# COMPAS invariants

COMPAS moves permission, not money. It is non-custodial. Delegated capacity is not a transfer to the delegate, and `remainingAuthorizedAmount` is not a wallet balance.

Purpose rules belong to COMPAS. Open Payments grants, actions, and limits are a separate layer. Do not call `MEDICATION` an Open Payments scope.

Never fake a successful Open Payments call. Throw until the gateway is real. Label fixtures `demo/test data`, and do not present them as live quotes or payments.

AI can classify. AI cannot authorize. Low confidence fails closed. Call `createOutgoingPayment` only after policy returns `ALLOW`.

```ts
if (!outgoingPaymentMayProceed(decision.outcome)) {
  return;
}
await gateway.createOutgoingPayment(input);
```

Keep the Interledger SDK behind `OpenPaymentsGateway`. Do not put health data in Open Payments metadata. Use opaque `compasMandateId`, `compasDecisionId`, and `externalReference` only.

Reuse the Mandate for every later context. Do not add a blockchain, a new app, or a library without a concrete need. Do not claim a simulated ARQ, Nequi, Bre-B, or other integration is real.

Copy any new AI coding prompt verbatim into `prompts/`. Update `AI_USAGE.md` when an AI tool's role changes materially.
